{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00634",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 0.77,
      "end_seconds": 14.68,
      "duration_seconds": 13.91,
      "text": "Sorry, sorry, we're late, the bus, and then Callum needed the toilet, and then I forgot the red book, so I've no idea what I've got here. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.55,
      "end_seconds": 25.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.88,
      "text": "No worries at all. Come in, sit down. Hello Callum, how old are you? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.2,
      "end_seconds": 27.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Four! ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.16,
      "end_seconds": 35.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.93,
      "text": "Four, brilliant. Dad, tell me what's been going on. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 36.17,
      "end_seconds": 52.41,
      "duration_seconds": 16.24,
      "text": "Right, so. He was sick in the night, Tuesday, no, Wednesday, it was bin day so Wednesday, and he's been sick three times. And then this morning the runs started."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.61,
      "end_seconds": 59.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "So vomiting since Wednesday night, and diarrhoea since this morning?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 62.36,
      "end_seconds": 72.27,
      "duration_seconds": 9.91,
      "text": "Yes. Well, the diarrhoea, it was before breakfast. Four times already today. Which is a lot for one small person."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.52,
      "end_seconds": 76.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Tummy hurts. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.47,
      "end_seconds": 83.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Does it, Callum? Show me where. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.64,
      "end_seconds": 87.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Here. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.02,
      "end_seconds": 93.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Okay. Is he drinking, Dad? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 95.19,
      "end_seconds": 106.56,
      "duration_seconds": 11.37,
      "text": "Little sips. He keeps asking for apple juice, and I've been, I don't know if I should be giving him that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.51,
      "end_seconds": 119.62,
      "duration_seconds": 12.11,
      "text": "A few sips of whatever he'll take is fine. What about wees, is he still having wet nappies, or pants, I mean, sorry? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 122.17,
      "end_seconds": 131.92,
      "duration_seconds": 9.75,
      "text": "Yes, I think so. Twice today, I'd say. Yes. His brother had it last week, it's going round the nursery. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.04,
      "end_seconds": 143.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "That helps me, thank you. Has Callum got any health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 145.22,
      "end_seconds": 157.71,
      "duration_seconds": 12.49,
      "text": "He has asthma, mild, he's got the brown inhaler for it. Well, he had it, I'm not sure where it went."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.87,
      "end_seconds": 171.46,
      "duration_seconds": 11.59,
      "text": "That's fine, we can sort that out another day. Let's have a look at him. Can I take your temperature, Callum? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.14,
      "end_seconds": 175.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Under my arm? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.45,
      "end_seconds": 190.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Under your arm, you've done this before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 191.93,
      "end_seconds": 194.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Is he warm? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.71,
      "end_seconds": 206.98,
      "duration_seconds": 10.27,
      "text": "Temperature 37.6, so just slightly raised, and his pulse is 108, which is normal for a four-year-old who's been vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 209.53,
      "end_seconds": 214.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Is that good? I never know what's good. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.32,
      "end_seconds": 228.5,
      "duration_seconds": 11.18,
      "text": "It's reassuring. Callum, lie back on the bed, I'm going to press your tummy. Tell me if it's sore. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.45,
      "end_seconds": 231.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Tickles! ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.65,
      "end_seconds": 253.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "His belly is soft, and he's not tender anywhere. There's nothing that worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 255.44,
      "end_seconds": 258.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "So what is it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.07,
      "end_seconds": 268.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "Together with the nursery and his brother, this looks like a tummy bug, gastroenteritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 270.16,
      "end_seconds": 275.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Does he need antibiotics? My mum says he'll need antibiotics. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.2,
      "end_seconds": 289.66,
      "duration_seconds": 12.46,
      "text": "No, they don't help with a stomach bug. What helps is fluids, a little and often. A few sips every few minutes rather than a big glass."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 290.47,
      "end_seconds": 296.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Little and often. I can do that. And food? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.53,
      "end_seconds": 304.99,
      "duration_seconds": 7.46,
      "text": "Plain, simple food when he asks for it. Nothing fatty. Don't force it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 307.59,
      "end_seconds": 311.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Right. How long does it last? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.17,
      "end_seconds": 329.24,
      "duration_seconds": 16.07,
      "text": "Most children are right within three to five days. If the diarrhoea is still going after a week, I'd like you to bring in a stool sample so we can test it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 330.35,
      "end_seconds": 333.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "In a pot? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.87,
      "end_seconds": 339.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "In a pot, yes. We'll give you one at reception. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 342.36,
      "end_seconds": 346.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Okay. And when do I worry? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.82,
      "end_seconds": 360.22,
      "duration_seconds": 12.4,
      "text": "If he's not weeing for eight hours, is very drowsy, vomits green, or has blood in the poo, take him to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 363.09,
      "end_seconds": 367.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Got it. I'll write it on my hand. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.42,
      "end_seconds": 373.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Good idea. Bye, Callum. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.8,
      "end_seconds": 376.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Bye! ~"
    }
  ]
}
